#: ../../../reuse/usb-using-balena-etcher-on-macos.txt:8
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"This part no longer applies because the Scheme option no longer exists in "
"recent macOS (since 2020).\n"
"\n"
"To ensure compatibility with Apple hardware, reformat the USB stick with the "
"GUID partition table. You can skip this part if you intend to use the USB "
"stick only with PC hardware:\n"
"\n"
"1. Launch the *Disk Utility* app from {menuselection}`Applications -> "
"Utilities` or from the Spotlight search.\n"
"\n"
"1. Insert your USB stick. It appears in the sidebar. Select it there.\n"
"\n"
"    You might need to enable the {menuselection}`View -> Show All Devices` "
"option.\n"
"\n"
"    :::{warning}\n"
"    Make sure to select the USB stick and **not** your internal macOS disk. "
"Both are listed.\n"
"    :::\n"
"\n"
"1. Select {guilabel}`Erase` from the toolbar.\n"
"\n"
"1. Set the format to *MS-DOS (FAT)* and the scheme to *GUID Partition Map*.\n"
"\n"
"1. Check that you've chosen the correct device and click {guilabel}`Erase`.\n"
"\n"
"1. Close the Disk Utility.\n"
"\n"
"Write the Ubuntu image to the USB stick:\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

